# 3DFlatter agent pointer

- Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) at session start for commands, boundaries, and architecture.
- Follow [docs/decisions/poc/0001-mesh-model-and-topology.md](docs/decisions/poc/0001-mesh-model-and-topology.md) for mesh, seam, and topology contracts.
- Plans: PoC [docs/plans/poc/](docs/plans/poc/README.md) · Product [docs/plans/product/](docs/plans/product/README.md) — not `.cursor/plans/`.
- Prefer minimal diffs; extend existing code in `src/logic/`; ask before architectural changes or new dependencies.
- Run `npm test` before marking work complete.
- Algorithmic Done ≠ green tests: follow [AGENTS.md — Algorithmic & slice Done criteria](AGENTS.md#algorithmic--slice-done-criteria).
- Tier B logic (mesh/topology/cuts/isolation/unfold): adversarial fixtures + red-before-green + Red Team QA audit before Done; next epic slice blocked until High/Critical closed or waived.
- Prefer small but topologically rich fixtures; reject tautological assertions (`size > 0`, renamed cylinder bands, tests that pass if a barrier channel is ignored).
